// compile-only: built-in globals (ShortcutInput, Clipboard, CurrentDate,
// Device, Ask) must not pick up a VariableName anywhere they're referenced.
// Native Shortcuts identifies them by Type alone; a VariableName makes
// Shortcuts treat them as a reference to a missing user-defined variable
// instead of the actual global, so the global's value never reaches the
// action. Covers the three places that encode a variable reference:
// a Variable-typed action argument, a conditional's input value, and an
// inline interpolation.

#include 'actions/contacts'

// Variable-typed action argument (action.go, makeActionParams)
const numbers = getPhoneNumbers(ShortcutInput)

// Conditional input value (shortcutgen.go, variableValueWithSerialization)
if ShortcutInput {
	nothing()
}

// Inline interpolation (shortcutgen.go, makeAttachmentValues)
text("Clipboard was: {Clipboard}")
